Z||000000||FieroKyle||11-27-2001||11:03 PM||||The motor that the Fiero came in. Not the SD4 or Standard's really nice quad 4 H.O.<P>But I guess posting any really fast 1/4 mile 4-cylinder times.<P>EDIT: Looking back the title, any modded Duke is no longer stock. The only way to make a Duke fast is to mod. So I am talking about 1/4 times of a modded Duke, but the one the car came in or the same engine from may be another Fiero or whatever car carried the 2.5L Duke with the same specs. I think you guys know what I mean, but may be not. Probably have all your heads spinning at this point. Its okay.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokylesig_1.gif">       <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT<p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jncomutt||11-27-2001||11:50 PM||||My 84 ran a whopping 17.2 at the track in PA.  LOL, I know there are much faster, but i just feel good being the fastest post so far.<P>Wait, i'm the only post so far....  Oh well, still makes me happy  =)||||reg||1
Z||000002||banditbalz||11-28-2001||12:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>My 84 ran a whopping 17.2 at the track in PA. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's a very respectible time for a duke... I guess you have the 4 speed Muncie with the performance ratio 4.10  I had one once. I still remember in college the day I raced a kid in a 2.8 firebird (auto) that his dad had bought him. We raced one time at a red light. At 100 km/h I was ahead of him. I don't expect to see any "stock" dukes running quicker than that. The Duke is a great "torque monster" of a motor. I could lay a patch of rubber far longer than I can in my 3.65 GT<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sunset_7.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||11-28-2001||12:14 AM||||I really want to get some times for my 84se. It has the 4.10 4 speed, fallen' off cat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">, K&N air filter, drilled airbox, few other little misc things, oh ya it also has an abusive driver (me! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">). I bet I can get high 8 sec 0-60. No idea about .25 mile.<P>Can burn all the way through 1st gear with a clutch dump, and do a nice bark into 2nd. <P>My 88 coupe auto could hit 0-60 in mid 9 secs. The DIS engine seems to pull a bit better at low RPM's.||||reg||6
Z||000004||AutoXdbdragSE||11-28-2001||12:55 AM||||MY 84 se does 0-60 in 8.8.. should be down t 8.5 after i tune it up for autocross, put the cat back on.. advance the timing 1 degree, and put on a acel coil.  1/4 no idea on time but my trap speed is 83 mph.. i'm guessing 17ish||||reg||1
