Z||000010||Pheagey||11-28-2001||08:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B> Maniak84 and I are looking to do the same thing except we're going to use about a 200 shot of nitrous!<P>Should make it go like a screamer for a few seconds...  Woo Hoo!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yea, and you migth want to add a 1" metal plate between you adn the engine...<P>I dont know what my time was but I got up to 72MPH on a 1/2mi.<P>I've spun thru 1st (over shootiong redline-not good), and barked a lil in 2nd. <P>Im running a '88 cuope, vacuum leak (somewhere), and trunk full of sh*t (proo exuces I know).<P>Mods: painted air intake cover=5HP+&lt;smerk&gt;.<P><P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed;<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageysfeiro<BR>"The car formaly know as, and has now reverted back to being known as, Pheagey's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000011||Master_Sushi||11-28-2001||01:58 PM||||I noticed after ditching my cat I lost a little low end power. But the car pulled allot better at high RPMS. I upshift at about 5400rpm. Anything over that and it just making loud noise, and dukes arnt exactly high RPM engines.<BR>I let my friend drive my fiero once. He had the thing in 2nd gear at 6200 rpm around a corner  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">. I was waiting to hear a rod go flying through my decklid. Was glad I spent the extra money to get mobil 1 15w-50. I thought 84's had rev limiters, I guess not though.<P>I am also thinking of geting a NOS system in the spring. I don't think the engine will last to long though. A 25 shot probably wouldn't kill the engine right away. If it does I really don't care, im parting out my car in the not to distant future. Maybe I'll but another duke and build the engine up. Would be fun!||||reg||14
